  "implemented": [
    "Fixed original GSA POST envelope/client metadata and exact trusteddevice/validate GET endpoints, keeping redirects/auth/cookies/cache/TLS/body limits/cancellation in the same transport.",
    "Fixed RFC5054 group2048/SHA256, secure32-byte a, cancellable s2k/s2k_fo PBKDF2, padded k/u/K/M1/M2 and noUsernameInX colon semantics.",
    "Mandatory server M2 and negotiation transcript HMAC (LE data lengths) before authenticated SPD CBC parse, exact app-token checksum and XYZ/16-byte-IV GCM tag before token parse.",
    "Actor busy covers actual handshake/connect calls. One in-memory five-minute trusted-device challenge is consumed once, validation restarts a fresh authenticated SRP then same Client.connect. No password disk/Keychain entry and no automatic/infinite2FA retry.",
    "Only serial metadata optional field is added to existing Anisette DTO for source-compatible old callers; Auth requires real provider metadata, never substitutes a fake serial or authorization flag.",
    "Token is delivered directly to same existing account Client.connect; the original session/team pin and secure record owner remain responsible for admission/persistence. No external session-valid flag."
  ],
  "actualDIInterface": {
    "type": "SelfRenewalDeveloperAuthentication actor",
    "initializer": "init(account: SelfRenewalDeveloperAccountClient, transport: any SelfRenewalDeveloperAccountTransport, freshAnisette: @Sendable () async throws -> SelfRenewalDeveloperAccountClient.Anisette, clock: @Sendable () -> Date = Date, random: @Sendable () throws -> Data = SecRandom-backed helper)",
